.TH FONTED 1
.SH NAME
fonted \- bitmap font editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/fonted
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I FontEd
is a port of the TempleOS 8x8 system font editor.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
A 16\(mu16 chart shows all 256 glyphs, seeded from the authentic
TempleOS system font, rendered live from the editable bitmaps; the
selected glyph blinks and is magnified in a blow-up grid where
individual pixels are painted.
Saving writes a hex dump in the original
.B FESave
format: one 64-bit word per glyph
.RB ( 0x%016X, ,
row 0 in the low byte, least-significant bit leftmost) with
.BI // c
comments for printable characters \(em paste-ready for the TempleOS
.BR Kernel/FontStd.HC .
.PP
The controls are:
.TF space
.TP
.B LMB or RMB on chart
Select glyph
.TP
.B LMB on blow-up
Set pixel (paints while dragged)
.TP
.B RMB on blow-up
Clear pixel (paints while dragged)
.TP
.B Arrow keys
Move the selection by \(+-1 (left/right) or \(+-16 (up/down)
.TP
.B Any printable key
Jump to that character's glyph
.TP
.B Ctrl-A
Save the hex dump
.TP
.B Esc
Save, then exit
.TP
.B Del
Exit without saving (the original's Shift-Esc)
.PD
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /tmp/temple-font.hex
Saved font dump.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/fonted.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
.SH BUGS
The original's
.B <CTRL-ALT-f>
main/aux system font toggle swaps the live console font and has no
Inferno equivalent; the banner is shown but the toggle does nothing.
